## Check a real task

1. Identify the exact Home Assistant version, the integration, the entity's capabilities and the person's permissions.
2. Follow the specification's states and acceptance checks, using invented data first.
3. Check keyboard use, narrow layouts, text resizing, reduced motion and the non-visual route. Record the browser and assistive technology you actually used.
4. Keep an automated example check, a native task test and a live device observation as three separate results. Do not report a check you have not run as a pass.
5. Keep the native route available when a private host changes or a capability is not supported.

The [native task accessibility](native-task-accessibility.html) and [compatibility register](compatibility-register.html) pages set out these limits in detail. The [work-package checklist](../community/guidance-work-package.html) records the implementation and verification evidence for this revision.

